    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In our new age of 21st-century-skills, collaboration and communication have been highlighted as skills which are essential to thrive in an unknown economic future (Griffin, McGaw, and Care, 2012). Vibe is a tool designed for late primary and secondary school classroom teachers, that measures student habits of collaboration and communication, and provides instructional guides when necessary. Vibe sees these skills as a learning goal -- an end unto itself -- and leverages the affordances of modern technology to collect and interpret formative data in a manner that reduces the time and attention demands on the teacher. The teacher is thus able to assess, give feedback, and plan her next steps in a data driven way - just as is done today in teaching traditional content knowledge. \r\nVibe takes the form of a set of student wearables paired with a visual interface (app) for the teacher and for student teams. Vibe’s biosensor technology measures student vocal participation and interaction. The teacher interface presents the data visually, in a manner that is easy to interpret and suggestions to help teachers facilitate effective collaborative work both real time and over time. The student group interface will encourage awareness of the collaborative process and support self assessment. Students will receive a select array of insights guided by the teacher.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
